{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CqWY5QxfU3wrb3KAP458g4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t// Package serve is the manigot daemon — the \"listener\" control plane\n2\t// described in docs/web-interface.md and the listener brief: a long-running\n3\t// `mg serve` process exposing a read-only control API over the existing\n4\t// in-process machinery (internal/job, internal/git, the mg jdi state machine,\n5\t// the session launcher), so any surface — a web UI, a native GUI, a future\n6\t// CLI — can attach to it as a client, from localhost or from a VPS.\n7\t//\n8\t// One package owns the daemon: the project registry, the HTTP server and its\n9\t// handlers, auth, the audit log, and the per-project serialization skeleton —\n10\t// mirroring how internal/session owns the session launcher. The scope of the\n11\t// v1 API is deliberately read-only (see the brief's out-of-scope list);\n12\t// mutating endpoints are a later job and inherit the serialization pattern\n13\t// established here.\n14\tpackage serve\n15\t\n16\timport (\n17\t\t\"encoding/json\"\n18\t\t\"errors\"\n19\t\t\"fmt\"\n20\t\t\"io\"\n21\t\t\"os\"\n22\t\t\"path/filepath\"\n23\t\t\"regexp\"\n24\t\n25\t\t\"github.com/lmuskalla/manigot/internal/config\"\n26\t\t\"github.com/lmuskalla/manigot/internal/fs\"\n27\t)\n28\t\n29\t// RegistryFileName is the name of the registry config file inside the\n30\t// manigot checkout's config/ directory.\n31\tconst RegistryFileName = \"serve.json\"\n32\t\n33\t// DefaultRegistryPath returns the default registry config location:\n34\t// <manigot checkout>/config/serve.json (config.Dir()). \"\" when the checkout\n35\t// cannot be located — the caller (mg serve) then reports a clear error.\n36\tfunc DefaultRegistryPath() string {\n37\t\tdir := config.Dir()\n38\t\tif dir == \"\" {\n39\t\t\treturn \"\"\n40\t\t}\n41\t\treturn filepath.Join(dir, \"serve.json\")\n42\t}\n43\t\n44\t// registryEntry is the on-disk JSON shape of one registry entry: an\n45\t// operator-chosen name (the URL segment the daemon serves it under) and its\n46\t// filesystem root. The flat-string form (\"projects\": [\"/abs/root\"]) is not\n47\t// supported — json.Unmarshal of a string into this struct fails naturally,\n48\t// which is exactly the \"no backwards compatibility\" behavior the brief calls\n49\t// for.\n50\ttype registryEntry struct {\n51\t\tName string `json:\"name\"`\n52\t\tPath string `json:\"path\"`\n53\t}\n54\t\n55\t// registryFile is the on-disk JSON shape of the registry config file.\n56\ttype registryFile struct {\n57\t\tProjects []registryEntry `json:\"projects\"`\n58\t}\n59\t\n60\t// Entry is one registered project: an operator-chosen name (the URL segment\n61\t// that resolves to it) and its absolute, cleaned filesystem root.\n62\ttype Entry struct {\n63\t\tName string\n64\t\tPath string\n65\t}\n66\t\n67\t// projectNamePattern is the URL-safe charset a registry entry's name must\n68\t// match: ASCII letters, digits, dot, underscore, hyphen. A name is served\n69\t// verbatim in /projects and matched byte-for-byte against incoming URL\n70\t// segments (see api.go's resolveProject), so keeping the charset\n71\t// conservative avoids any ambiguity from encoding, case-folding, or reserved\n72\t// URL characters — a stricter requirement than validSegment's structural\n73\t// no-traversal/no-separator discipline, which this also reuses.\n74\tvar projectNamePattern = regexp.MustCompile(`^[A-Za-z0-9._-]+$`)\n75\t\n76\t// validProjectName reports whether name is an acceptable registry entry\n77\t// name: validSegment's structural discipline (non-empty, not \".\" or \"..\", no\n78\t// path separator, no NUL) plus the conservative URL-safe charset above.\n79\tfunc validProjectName(name string) bool {\n80\t\treturn validSegment(name) && projectNamePattern.MatchString(name)\n81\t}\n82\t\n83\t// Registry is the daemon's explicit list of named project entries. It is\n84\t// read once at startup from a config file — no scanning, no auto-adopting\n85\t// directories the daemon finds. Changing the registered entries means\n86\t// editing the config file and restarting (v1). Every handler resolves ONLY\n87\t// against these entries via Entries()/Project() — the single choke point the\n88\t// zero-path-inputs enforcement (see api.go's resolution helpers) builds on.\n89\ttype Registry struct {\n90\t\tentries []Entry // name + absolute, cleaned path, in config-file order\n91\t}\n92\t\n93\t// LoadRegistry reads the registry config file at path and validates every\n94\t// entry. A missing file is an empty registry, not an error (a fresh checkout\n95\t// simply has nothing registered yet). An unreadable-but-present file, an\n96\t// unparseable file, an invalid or duplicate name, a duplicate path, or an\n97\t// entry whose path is not an existing directory is an error — a broken\n98\t// registry must never silently serve a subset.\n99\t//\n100\t// Each entry's name must be non-empty, a single URL-safe path segment\n101\t// (validProjectName), and unique across the registry. Each entry's path must\n102\t// exist as a directory; a root without docs/ is accepted (it lists no jobs\n103\t// rather than failing startup) — the caller may warn about it, see\n104\t// (*Registry).WarnMissingDocs. Two entries registering the same path (under\n105\t// different names) are also refused: a path is intended to be reachable\n106\t// under exactly one operator-chosen identity, and rejecting keeps the\n107\t// \"refuse to start on anything surprising\" discipline the rest of the\n108\t// registry's validation follows, rather than silently picking one name over\n109\t// the other.\n110\tfunc LoadRegistry(path string) (*Registry, error) {\n111\t\tdata, err := os.ReadFile(path)\n112\t\tif err != nil {\n113\t\t\tif os.IsNotExist(err) {\n114\t\t\t\treturn &Registry{}, nil\n115\t\t\t}\n116\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"read registry %s: %w\", path, err)\n117\t\t}\n118\t\n119\t\tvar raw registryFile\n120\t\tif err := json.Unmarshal(data, &raw); err != nil {\n121\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"parse registry %s: %w\", path, err)\n122\t\t}\n123\t\n124\t\treg := &Registry{}\n125\t\tseenNames := make(map[string]bool)\n126\t\tseenPaths := make(map[string]string) // abs path -> the name that claimed it\n127\t\tfor _, e := range raw.Projects {\n128\t\t\tif !validProjectName(e.Name) {\n129\t\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"registry %s: entry name %q is invalid — it must be non-empty, a single URL-safe path segment (%s), not \\\".\\\" or \\\"..\\\"\", path, e.Name, projectNamePattern.String())\n130\t\t\t}\n131\t\t\tif seenNames[e.Name] {\n132\t\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"registry %s: duplicate entry name %q\", path, e.Name)\n133\t\t\t}\n134\t\n135\t\t\tabs, err := filepath.Abs(e.Path)\n136\t\t\tif err != nil {\n137\t\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"registry %s: entry %q: resolve %q: %w\", path, e.Name, e.Path, err)\n138\t\t\t}\n139\t\t\tabs = filepath.Clean(abs)\n140\t\t\tif other, ok := seenPaths[abs]; ok {\n141\t\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"registry %s: entry %q and %q both register path %q\", path, other, e.Name, abs)\n142\t\t\t}\n143\t\t\tinfo, err := os.Stat(abs)\n144\t\t\tif err != nil {\n145\t\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"registry %s: entry %q: %q is not an existing directory: %w\", path, e.Name, e.Path, err)\n146\t\t\t}\n147\t\t\tif !info.IsDir() {\n148\t\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"registry %s: entry %q: %q is not a directory\", path, e.Name, e.Path)\n149\t\t\t}\n150\t\n151\t\t\tseenNames[e.Name] = true\n152\t\t\tseenPaths[abs] = e.Name\n153\t\t\treg.entries = append(reg.entries, Entry{Name: e.Name, Path: abs})\n154\t\t}\n155\t\treturn reg, nil\n156\t}\n157\t\n158\t// Entries returns an ordered copy of the registered entries (name + path).\n159\t// The copy guarantees a caller cannot mutate the registry's internal slice.\n160\tfunc (r *Registry) Entries() []Entry {\n161\t\treturn append([]Entry(nil), r.entries...)\n162\t}\n163\t\n164\t// Projects returns an ordered copy of the registered project roots' paths.\n165\t// The copy guarantees a caller cannot mutate the registry's internal slice.\n166\tfunc (r *Registry) Projects() []string {\n167\t\tpaths := make([]string, len(r.entries))\n168\t\tfor i, e := range r.entries {\n169\t\t\tpaths[i] = e.Path\n170\t\t}\n171\t\treturn paths\n172\t}\n173\t\n174\t// Project resolves a URL project segment against the registered entries by\n175\t// configured name ONLY — names are validated unique at load time, so there\n176\t// is no ambiguity to resolve. Nothing is ever joined into a filesystem path\n177\t// here — the returned root IS one of the registered paths, never a\n178\t// derivation from the input. ok is false when the segment matches no entry's\n179\t// name.\n180\tfunc (r *Registry) Project(segment string) (string, bool) {\n181\t\tfor _, e := range r.entries {\n182\t\t\tif e.Name == segment {\n183\t\t\t\treturn e.Path, true\n184\t\t\t}\n185\t\t}\n186\t\treturn \"\", false\n187\t}\n188\t\n189\t// WarnMissingDocs writes a warning line for every registered root without a\n190\t// docs/ directory to w — the \"a registered project needs docs/ for jobs, but\n191\t// a root without docs/ lists no jobs rather than failing startup\" behavior\n192\t// the brief calls for. w may be nil (no warnings).\n193\tfunc (r *Registry) WarnMissingDocs(w io.Writer) {\n194\t\tfor _, e := range r.entries {\n195\t\t\tif !fs.IsDir(filepath.Join(e.Path, \"docs\")) {\n196\t\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(w, \"Warning: registered project %s (%s) has no docs/ directory — it will list no jobs.\\n\", e.Name, e.Path)\n197\t\t\t}\n198\t\t}\n199\t}\n200\t\n201\t// ErrNoRegistryPath is returned by mg serve when the registry path cannot be\n202\t// determined (no --registry flag and the manigot checkout cannot be located).\n203\tvar ErrNoRegistryPath = errors.New(\"cannot determine the registry config location (set $MANIGOT_HOME or pass --registry)\")\n204\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ba948ea7-a157-4c42-8eb1-077540d9946d","uuid":"3c561e89-8f5b-4d5b-9083-6b664701ca29","timestamp":"2026-08-28T20:29:09.717Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/src/internal/serve/registry.go","content":"// Package serve is the manigot daemon — the \"listener\" control plane\n// described in docs/web-interface.md and the listener brief: a long-running\n// `mg serve` process exposing a read-only control API over the existing\n// in-process machinery (internal/job, internal/git, the mg jdi state machine,\n// the session launcher), so any surface — a web UI, a native GUI, a future\n// CLI — can attach to it as a client, from localhost or from a VPS.\n//\n// One package owns the daemon: the project registry, the HTTP server and its\n// handlers, auth, the audit log, and the per-project serialization skeleton —\n// mirroring how internal/session owns the session launcher. The scope of the\n// v1 API is deliberately read-only (see the brief's out-of-scope list);\n// mutating endpoints are a later job and inherit the serialization pattern\n// established here.\npackage serve\n\nimport (\n\t\"encoding/json\"\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"io\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\t\"regexp\"\n\n\t\"github.com/lmuskalla/manigot/internal/config\"\n\t\"github.com/lmuskalla/manigot/internal/fs\"\n)\n\n// RegistryFileName is the name of the registry config file inside the\n// manigot checkout's config/ directory.\nconst RegistryFileName = \"serve.json\"\n\n// DefaultRegistryPath returns the default registry config location:\n// <manigot checkout>/config/serve.json (config.Dir()). \"\" when the checkout\n// cannot be located — the caller (mg serve) then reports a clear error.\nfunc DefaultRegistryPath() string {\n\tdir := config.Dir()\n\tif dir == \"\" {\n\t\treturn \"\"\n\t}\n\treturn filepath.Join(dir, \"serve.json\")\n}\n\n// registryEntry is the on-disk JSON shape of one registry entry: an\n// operator-chosen name (the URL segment the daemon serves it under) and its\n// filesystem root. The flat-string form (\"projects\": [\"/abs/root\"]) is not\n// supported — json.Unmarshal of a string into this struct fails naturally,\n// which is exactly the \"no backwards compatibility\" behavior the brief calls\n// for.\ntype registryEntry struct {\n\tName string `json:\"name\"`\n\tPath string `json:\"path\"`\n}\n\n// registryFile is the on-disk JSON shape of the registry config file.\ntype registryFile struct {\n\tProjects []registryEntry `json:\"projects\"`\n}\n\n// Entry is one registered project: an operator-chosen name (the URL segment\n// that resolves to it) and its absolute, cleaned filesystem root.\ntype Entry struct {\n\tName string\n\tPath string\n}\n\n// projectNamePattern is the URL-safe charset a registry entry's name must\n// match: ASCII letters, digits, dot, underscore, hyphen. A name is served\n// verbatim in /projects and matched byte-for-byte against incoming URL\n// segments (see api.go's resolveProject), so keeping the charset\n// conservative avoids any ambiguity from encoding, case-folding, or reserved\n// URL characters — a stricter requirement than validSegment's structural\n// no-traversal/no-separator discipline, which this also reuses.\nvar projectNamePattern = regexp.MustCompile(`^[A-Za-z0-9._-]+$`)\n\n// validProjectName reports whether name is an acceptable registry entry\n// name: validSegment's structural discipline (non-empty, not \".\" or \"..\", no\n// path separator, no NUL) plus the conservative URL-safe charset above.\nfunc validProjectName(name string) bool {\n\treturn validSegment(name) && projectNamePattern.MatchString(name)\n}\n\n// Registry is the daemon's explicit list of named project entries. It is\n// read once at startup from a config file — no scanning, no auto-adopting\n// directories the daemon finds. Changing the registered entries means\n// editing the config file and restarting (v1). Every handler resolves ONLY\n// against these entries via Entries()/Project() — the single choke point the\n// zero-path-inputs enforcement (see api.go's resolution helpers) builds on.\ntype Registry struct {\n\tentries []Entry // name + absolute, cleaned path, in config-file order\n}\n\n// LoadRegistry reads the registry config file at path and validates every\n// entry. A missing file is an empty registry, not an error (a fresh checkout\n// simply has nothing registered yet). An unreadable-but-present file, an\n// unparseable file, an invalid or duplicate name, a duplicate path, or an\n// entry whose path is not an existing directory is an error — a broken\n// registry must never silently serve a subset.\n//\n// Each entry's name must be non-empty, a single URL-safe path segment\n// (validProjectName), and unique across the registry. Each entry's path must\n// exist as a directory; a root without docs/ is accepted (it lists no jobs\n// rather than failing startup) — the caller may warn about it, see\n// (*Registry).WarnMissingDocs. Two entries registering the same path (under\n// different names) are also refused: a path is intended to be reachable\n// under exactly one operator-chosen identity, and rejecting keeps the\n// \"refuse to start on anything surprising\" discipline the rest of the\n// registry's validation follows, rather than silently picking one name over\n// the other.\nfunc LoadRegistry(path string) (*Registry, error) {\n\tdata, err := os.ReadFile(path)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tif os.IsNotExist(err) {\n\t\t\treturn &Registry{}, nil\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"read registry %s: %w\", path, err)\n\t}\n\n\tvar raw registryFile\n\tif err := json.Unmarshal(data, &raw); err != nil {\n\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"parse registry %s: %w\", path, err)\n\t}\n\n\treg := &Registry{}\n\tseenNames := make(map[string]bool)\n\tseenPaths := make(map[string]string) // abs path -> the name that claimed it\n\tfor _, e := range raw.Projects {\n\t\tif !validProjectName(e.Name) {\n\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"registry %s: entry name %q is invalid — it must be non-empty, a single URL-safe path segment (%s), not \\\".\\\" or \\\"..\\\"\", path, e.Name, projectNamePattern.String())\n\t\t}\n\t\tif seenNames[e.Name] {\n\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"registry %s: duplicate entry name %q\", path, e.Name)\n\t\t}\n\n\t\tabs, err := filepath.Abs(e.Path)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"registry %s: entry %q: resolve %q: %w\", path, e.Name, e.Path, err)\n\t\t}\n\t\tabs = filepath.Clean(abs)\n\t\tif other, ok := seenPaths[abs]; ok {\n\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"registry %s: entry %q and %q both register path %q\", path, other, e.Name, abs)\n\t\t}\n\t\tinfo, err := os.Stat(abs)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"registry %s: entry %q: %q is not an existing directory: %w\", path, e.Name, e.Path, err)\n\t\t}\n\t\tif !info.IsDir() {\n\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"registry %s: entry %q: %q is not a directory\", path, e.Name, e.Path)\n\t\t}\n\n\t\tseenNames[e.Name] = true\n\t\tseenPaths[abs] = e.Name\n\t\treg.entries = append(reg.entries, Entry{Name: e.Name, Path: abs})\n\t}\n\treturn reg, nil\n}\n\n// Entries returns an ordered copy of the registered entries (name + path).\n// The copy guarantees a caller cannot mutate the registry's internal slice.\nfunc (r *Registry) Entries() []Entry {\n\treturn append([]Entry(nil), r.entries...)\n}\n\n// Projects returns an ordered copy of the registered project roots' paths.\n// The copy guarantees a caller cannot mutate the registry's internal slice.\nfunc (r *Registry) Projects() []string {\n\tpaths := make([]string, len(r.entries))\n\tfor i, e := range r.entries {\n\t\tpaths[i] = e.Path\n\t}\n\treturn paths\n}\n\n// Project resolves a URL project segment against the registered entries by\n// configured name ONLY — names are validated unique at load time, so there\n// is no ambiguity to resolve. Nothing is ever joined into a filesystem path\n// here — the returned root IS one of the registered paths, never a\n// derivation from the input. ok is false when the segment matches no entry's\n// name.\nfunc (r *Registry) Project(segment string) (string, bool) {\n\tfor _, e := range r.entries {\n\t\tif e.Name == segment {\n\t\t\treturn e.Path, true\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn \"\", false\n}\n\n// WarnMissingDocs writes a warning line for every registered root without a\n// docs/ directory to w — the \"a registered project needs docs/ for jobs, but\n// a root without docs/ lists no jobs rather than failing startup\" behavior\n// the brief calls for. w may be nil (no warnings).\nfunc (r *Registry) WarnMissingDocs(w io.Writer) {\n\tfor _, e := range r.entries {\n\t\tif !fs.IsDir(filepath.Join(e.Path, \"docs\")) {\n\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(w, \"Warning: registered project %s (%s) has no docs/ directory — it will list no jobs.\\n\", e.Name, e.Path)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n}\n\n// ErrNoRegistryPath is returned by mg serve when the registry path cannot be\n// determined (no --registry flag and the manigot checkout cannot be located).\nvar ErrNoRegistryPath = errors.New(\"cannot determine the registry config location (set $MANIGOT_HOME or pass --registry)\")\n","numLines":204,"startLine":1,"totalLines":204}}}
