{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1787952140714,"sessionID":"ses_fb5dcd7a6ffeSGBPKFVeVpziRm","part":{"id":"prt_04a4091a8001EeEOvSaAZtI7oE","messageID":"msg_04a4088e6001IEaiOYFgkBVokm","sessionID":"ses_fb5dcd7a6ffeSGBPKFVeVpziRm","snapshot":"","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787952140850,"sessionID":"ses_fb5dcd7a6ffeSGBPKFVeVpziRm","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_c851f719a5af48b785b4752f","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/AGENTS.md","offset":509,"limit":130},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/AGENTS.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n509: ### Listener / control plane\n510: \n511: `mg serve` is the listener: a long-running daemon that exposes a **read-only**\n512: control API over a registry of project roots, so any surface — a web UI, a\n513: native GUI, a future CLI — can attach to it as a client, from localhost or\n514: from a VPS. It is job one of the control-plane sequence (`mg serve` + project\n515: registry + read-only API + localhost default + audit log + serialization\n516: skeleton); mutating endpoints, live run supervision with streamed logs, and\n517: any frontend are later jobs. The daemon is additive — the TUI stays\n518: in-process and every existing command keeps working untouched — and it is a\n519: **new trust boundary** with root-adjacent power (it drives docker and git and\n520: holds subscription credentials), so the v1 surface is deliberately read-only\n521: and the security invariants below are non-negotiable.\n522: \n523: - **Project registry.** An explicit config file, `<checkout>/config/serve.json`\n524:   (overridable via `--registry`), holding\n525:   `{\"projects\": [{\"name\": \"my-project\", \"path\": \"/abs/root\"}, ...]}` — each\n526:   entry an operator-chosen `name` (the URL segment the project is served\n527:   under) plus its `path`. No scanning, no auto-adopting directories the\n528:   daemon finds. Registrations are read once at startup; changing them means\n529:   editing the file and restarting (v1). Each entry is validated at startup:\n530:   `name` non-empty, a single URL-safe path segment (no `/` or `\\`, not `.` or\n531:   `..`, charset `[A-Za-z0-9._-]`), unique across the registry; `path` an\n532:   existing directory. A bad entry — an invalid or duplicate name, a duplicate\n533:   path, or a nonexistent directory — refuses the whole daemon to start, never\n534:   silently serving a subset; a root without `docs/` is accepted (it lists no\n535:   jobs rather than failing startup). Every handler resolves ONLY against the\n536:   registered entries, matching a URL segment by configured `name` — the\n537:   single choke point the zero-path-inputs rule builds on.\n538: - **Read-only API.** The state the TUI renders, over HTTP as JSON + raw\n539:   markdown (never ANSI): `GET /health` (version, docker image present,\n540:   per-profile readiness), `GET /projects`, `GET /projects/<p>/jobs` (the\n541:   TUI's info design — id/status/stage/type/date/title — plus per-job mg-jdi\n542:   state), `GET /projects/<p>/jobs/<j>/files/<brief|tasks|implementation|verdict>`,\n543:   `GET /projects/<p>/jobs/<j>/jdi` (status + `run.log` + `session.log` tails),\n544:   `GET /projects/<p>/jobs/<j>/diff` (the `mg diff` quick eyeball, `?full=1`\n545:   for the patch), and `GET /projects/<p>/agents` (name + description only).\n546: - **Binding + auth.** Binds `127.0.0.1:8080` by default, tokenless — the\n547:   machine's own user is the trust boundary, as it is for the CLI. A\n548:   non-loopback bind (neither 127.0.0.0/8 nor `::1`) REQUIRES a bearer token\n549:   (`--token`, else `$MG_SERVE_TOKEN` via the config/env layer) or the daemon\n550:   refuses to start — the guard is unskippable, there is no flag that turns it\n551:   off. When configured, every request must carry `Authorization: Bearer\n552:   <token>`, compared in constant time. TLS is the reverse proxy's job\n553:   (Caddy/nginx) — the daemon always serves plain HTTP and never terminates\n554:   TLS, the only safe posture behind a proxy. Tokens are configured\n555:   out-of-band; the API never issues, creates, or returns one.\n556: - **Audit trail.** Every request is logged — timestamp, client IP, method +\n557:   path, auth outcome (authed / tokenless / 401), response status — to the\n558:   daemon's stderr by default. The Authorization header, the token, and request\n559:   bodies are never logged.\n560: - **Security invariants.** (1) **Zero path inputs** — URL segments are\n561:   validated as plain identifiers and matched against the registry / discovered\n562:   jobs / the file whitelist; they are never joined into filesystem paths, and\n563:   traversal in any encoding is rejected. (2) **Credentials never returned** —\n564:   no `.env` content, no keys, no tokens in any response, ever (enforced by\n565:   tests over the whole surface). (3) **Per-project serialization** —\n566:   `serve.ProjectLocks` (keyed by registered root) is the concurrency pattern\n567:   job two's mutating handlers MUST use; `internal/git` has no locking today,\n568:   and v1 read endpoints deliberately take no locks.\n569: \n570: ### Config files\n571: \n572: - `manigot/.env` (gitignored) — credentials and defaults for the profiles\n573:   (`CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN`/`CLAUDE_ACCOUNT_UUID`/`CLAUDE_EMAIL`/\n574:   `CLAUDE_ORG_UUID` for claude-pro, `ZHIPU_API_KEY` + `OPENCODE_ZAI_MODEL`\n575:   for zai, `OPENCODE_API_KEY` + `OPENCODE_GO_MODEL` for opencode-go,\n576:   `OPENCODE_API_KEY` + `OPENCODE_ZEN_MODEL` for opencode-zen,\n577:   `OPENCODE_API_KEY` + `OPENCODE_ZEN_FREE_MODEL` for opencode-zen-free, and\n578:   `MANIGOT_PROFILE` — the default profile shared between CLI and TUI), plus\n579:   `OPENCODE_THEME` — the global OpenCode theme (set via `mg theme`), shared\n580:   across every OpenCode profile rather than pinned per-profile like the\n581:   `OPENCODE_*_MODEL` keys — and the optional ntfy push-notification keys\n582:   `NTFY_URL`/`NTFY_TOPIC`/`NTFY_TOKEN` for `mg jdi` (see the `mg jdi` section\n583:   — `NTFY_TOPIC` unset means no notifications at all).\n584:   Written by `mg setup`/`mg profiles`/`mg theme`/the TUI settings screen; read\n585:   via `config.GetEnv`/`EnvValue`. Never committed.\n586:   Key forwarding is pinned per profile (test-pinned in `internal/session`):\n587:   only `zai` forwards `ZHIPU_API_KEY` into its container, only `opencode-go`\n588:   forwards `OPENCODE_API_KEY`, and `claude-pro` forwards the OAuth token +\n589:   account UUIDs. Consequence for the `shot` render tool (docs/PLAYWRIGHT.md):\n590:   its `--describe` vision layer needs `ZHIPU_API_KEY` in the session env, so\n591:   it works under `zai` today; other profiles get a clear \"no key\" error and\n592:   fall back to the model-free render report. The perception matrix may later\n593:   widen the forwarding (see the job's probe protocol) — a one-line\n594:   `OpenCodeKeys` change plus its tests, deliberately not made pre-matrix.\n595: - `config/profiles.json` (gitignored) — the user-defined profile store: the\n596:   profiles created with `mg profiles add`, each a full definition (tool,\n597:   auth keys, model env/default) merged after the built-in table by\n598:   `config.Profiles()`/`ProfileByID()`. A missing or corrupt file degrades to\n599:   \"built-ins only\"; id collisions are rejected at write time. Built-ins are\n600:   compiled in, never stored here.\n601: - `config/tui-settings.json` (gitignored) — the TUI's personal preferences:\n602:   which editor opens `brief.md`, the recent-activity count, and which\n603:   terminal spawns a session (used only when the TUI is not inside tmux —\n604:   inside tmux the launch is always a tmux split pane, regardless of the\n605:   setting). The terminal override is the default every launch path falls\n606:   back to — the TUI passes it explicitly, and CLI paths like `mg done`'s\n607:   git-solver handoff resolve it via `launch.TerminalSetting`, so the same\n608:   setting applies everywhere, not just from the TUI. Missing is not an error\n609:   — every reader falls back to defaults.\n610: - `.manigot/manigot.json` (in the target project, committable) — project\n611:   conventions: `baseBranch` (the ref new job branches are cut from and\n612:   finished jobs are merged into, default `main`) and `jobBranchPrefix` (the\n613:   namespace job branches live under, default empty). Read by `mg job`/`mg\n614:   done`/`mg delete` via `internal/project` and by the TUI.\n615: - `.manigot/` (in the target project) — host-side tooling state only:\n616:   the committable `manigot.json` settings and the gitignored\n617:   `.manigot/jdi-status/` mg-jdi run state (removed when a job is finished,\n618:   deleted, or its orphaned worktree cleaned up). Agents must treat it like\n619:   any other tool-managed state: read the settings file if needed, never edit\n620:   either path by hand.\n621: \n622: ## Commands\n623: - `make build` — build the image (skips if already built)\n624: - `make rebuild` — force rebuild with no cache, after a Claude Code / OpenCode update\n625: - `make mg` — build the host-side `bin/mg` binary\n626: - `make install` / `make uninstall` — symlink the single `mg` binary into\n627:   `PREFIX/bin` (default `~/.local/bin`)\n628: - `mg` — start an isolated session from inside any project directory; `docs/`\n629:   is optional (see Architecture above)\n630: - `mg --profile <name>` — same, but under the given subscription profile\n631:   (`claude-pro`/`zai`/`opencode-go`/`opencode-zen`/`opencode-zen-free`); `--tool` is accepted as a legacy alias\n632: - `mg profiles [name|add|rm]` — list the profiles (and which is the default),\n633:   set the default bare `mg` uses, pick it interactively (no name, on a TTY),\n634:   or manage your own user-defined profiles with `add`/`rm`\n635:   (stored in `config/profiles.json`)\n636: - `mg theme [name]` — show or set manigot's global OpenCode theme\n637:   (`OPENCODE_THEME`, shared across every OpenCode profile), or pick it\n638:   interactively (no name, on a TTY) from a reference list of OpenCode's known\n\n(Showing lines 509-638 of 773. Use offset=639 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"### Listener / control plane\n\n`mg serve` is the listener: a long-running daemon that exposes a **read-only**\ncontrol API over a registry of project roots, so any surface — a web UI, a\nnative GUI, a future CLI — can attach to it as a client, from localhost or\nfrom a VPS. It is job one of the control-plane sequence (`mg serve` + project\nregistry + read-only API + localhost default + audit log + serialization\nskeleton); mutating endpoints, live run supervision with streamed logs, and\nany frontend are later jobs. The daemon is additive — the TUI stays\nin-process and every existing command keeps working untouched — and it is a\n**new trust boundary** with root-adjacent power (it drives docker and git and\nholds subscription credentials), so the v1 surface is deliberately read-only\nand the security invariants below are non-negotiable.\n\n- **Project registry.** An explicit config file, `<checkout>/config/serve.json`\n  (overridable via `--registry`), holding\n  `{\"projects\": [{\"name\": \"my-project\", \"path\": \"/abs/root\"}, ...]}` — each\n  entry an operator-chosen `name` (the URL segment the project is served\n  under) plus its `path`. No scanning, no auto-adopting directories the\n  daemon finds. Registrations are read once at startup; changing them means","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/AGENTS.md","text":"### Listener / control plane\n\n`mg serve` is the listener: a long-running daemon that exposes a **read-only**\ncontrol API over a registry of project roots, so any surface — a web UI, a\nnative GUI, a future CLI — can attach to it as a client, from localhost or\nfrom a VPS. It is job one of the control-plane sequence (`mg serve` + project\nregistry + read-only API + localhost default + audit log + serialization\nskeleton); mutating endpoints, live run supervision with streamed logs, and\nany frontend are later jobs. The daemon is additive — the TUI stays\nin-process and every existing command keeps working untouched — and it is a\n**new trust boundary** with root-adjacent power (it drives docker and git and\nholds subscription credentials), so the v1 surface is deliberately read-only\nand the security invariants below are non-negotiable.\n\n- **Project registry.** An explicit config file, `<checkout>/config/serve.json`\n  (overridable via `--registry`), holding\n  `{\"projects\": [{\"name\": \"my-project\", \"path\": \"/abs/root\"}, ...]}` — each\n  entry an operator-chosen `name` (the URL segment the project is served\n  under) plus its `path`. No scanning, no auto-adopting directories the\n  daemon finds. Registrations are read once at startup; changing them means\n  editing the file and restarting (v1). Each entry is validated at startup:\n  `name` non-empty, a single URL-safe path segment (no `/` or `\\`, not `.` or\n  `..`, charset `[A-Za-z0-9._-]`), unique across the registry; `path` an\n  existing directory. A bad entry — an invalid or duplicate name, a duplicate\n  path, or a nonexistent directory — refuses the whole daemon to start, never\n  silently serving a subset; a root without `docs/` is accepted (it lists no\n  jobs rather than failing startup). Every handler resolves ONLY against the\n  registered entries, matching a URL segment by configured `name` — the\n  single choke point the zero-path-inputs rule builds on.\n- **Read-only API.** The state the TUI renders, over HTTP as JSON + raw\n  markdown (never ANSI): `GET /health` (version, docker image present,\n  per-profile readiness), `GET /projects`, `GET /projects/<p>/jobs` (the\n  TUI's info design — id/status/stage/type/date/title — plus per-job mg-jdi\n  state), `GET /projects/<p>/jobs/<j>/files/<brief|tasks|implementation|verdict>`,\n  `GET /projects/<p>/jobs/<j>/jdi` (status + `run.log` + `session.log` tails),\n  `GET /projects/<p>/jobs/<j>/diff` (the `mg diff` quick eyeball, `?full=1`\n  for the patch), and `GET /projects/<p>/agents` (name + description only).\n- **Binding + auth.** Binds `127.0.0.1:8080` by default, tokenless — the\n  machine's own user is the trust boundary, as it is for the CLI. A\n  non-loopback bind (neither 127.0.0.0/8 nor `::1`) REQUIRES a bearer token\n  (`--token`, else `$MG_SERVE_TOKEN` via the config/env layer) or the daemon\n  refuses to start — the guard is unskippable, there is no flag that turns it\n  off. When configured, every request must carry `Authorization: Bearer\n  <token>`, compared in constant time. TLS is the reverse proxy's job\n  (Caddy/nginx) — the daemon always serves plain HTTP and never terminates\n  TLS, the only safe posture behind a proxy. Tokens are configured\n  out-of-band; the API never issues, creates, or returns one.\n- **Audit trail.** Every request is logged — timestamp, client IP, method +\n  path, auth outcome (authed / tokenless / 401), response status — to the\n  daemon's stderr by default. The Authorization header, the token, and request\n  bodies are never logged.\n- **Security invariants.** (1) **Zero path inputs** — URL segments are\n  validated as plain identifiers and matched against the registry / discovered\n  jobs / the file whitelist; they are never joined into filesystem paths, and\n  traversal in any encoding is rejected. (2) **Credentials never returned** —\n  no `.env` content, no keys, no tokens in any response, ever (enforced by\n  tests over the whole surface). (3) **Per-project serialization** —\n  `serve.ProjectLocks` (keyed by registered root) is the concurrency pattern\n  job two's mutating handlers MUST use; `internal/git` has no locking today,\n  and v1 read endpoints deliberately take no locks.\n\n### Config files\n\n- `manigot/.env` (gitignored) — credentials and defaults for the profiles\n  (`CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN`/`CLAUDE_ACCOUNT_UUID`/`CLAUDE_EMAIL`/\n  `CLAUDE_ORG_UUID` for claude-pro, `ZHIPU_API_KEY` + `OPENCODE_ZAI_MODEL`\n  for zai, `OPENCODE_API_KEY` + `OPENCODE_GO_MODEL` for opencode-go,\n  `OPENCODE_API_KEY` + `OPENCODE_ZEN_MODEL` for opencode-zen,\n  `OPENCODE_API_KEY` + `OPENCODE_ZEN_FREE_MODEL` for opencode-zen-free, and\n  `MANIGOT_PROFILE` — the default profile shared between CLI and TUI), plus\n  `OPENCODE_THEME` — the global OpenCode theme (set via `mg theme`), shared\n  across every OpenCode profile rather than pinned per-profile like the\n  `OPENCODE_*_MODEL` keys — and the optional ntfy push-notification keys\n  `NTFY_URL`/`NTFY_TOPIC`/`NTFY_TOKEN` for `mg jdi` (see the `mg jdi` section\n  — `NTFY_TOPIC` unset means no notifications at all).\n  Written by `mg setup`/`mg profiles`/`mg theme`/the TUI settings screen; read\n  via `config.GetEnv`/`EnvValue`. Never committed.\n  Key forwarding is pinned per profile (test-pinned in `internal/session`):\n  only `zai` forwards `ZHIPU_API_KEY` into its container, only `opencode-go`\n  forwards `OPENCODE_API_KEY`, and `claude-pro` forwards the OAuth token +\n  account UUIDs. Consequence for the `shot` render tool (docs/PLAYWRIGHT.md):\n  its `--describe` vision layer needs `ZHIPU_API_KEY` in the session env, so\n  it works under `zai` today; other profiles get a clear \"no key\" error and\n  fall back to the model-free render report. The perception matrix may later\n  widen the forwarding (see the job's probe protocol) — a one-line\n  `OpenCodeKeys` change plus its tests, deliberately not made pre-matrix.\n- `config/profiles.json` (gitignored) — the user-defined profile store: the\n  profiles created with `mg profiles add`, each a full definition (tool,\n  auth keys, model env/default) merged after the built-in table by\n  `config.Profiles()`/`ProfileByID()`. A missing or corrupt file degrades to\n  \"built-ins only\"; id collisions are rejected at write time. Built-ins are\n  compiled in, never stored here.\n- `config/tui-settings.json` (gitignored) — the TUI's personal preferences:\n  which editor opens `brief.md`, the recent-activity count, and which\n  terminal spawns a session (used only when the TUI is not inside tmux —\n  inside tmux the launch is always a tmux split pane, regardless of the\n  setting). The terminal override is the default every launch path falls\n  back to — the TUI passes it explicitly, and CLI paths like `mg done`'s\n  git-solver handoff resolve it via `launch.TerminalSetting`, so the same\n  setting applies everywhere, not just from the TUI. Missing is not an error\n  — every reader falls back to defaults.\n- `.manigot/manigot.json` (in the target project, committable) — project\n  conventions: `baseBranch` (the ref new job branches are cut from and\n  finished jobs are merged into, default `main`) and `jobBranchPrefix` (the\n  namespace job branches live under, default empty). Read by `mg job`/`mg\n  done`/`mg delete` via `internal/project` and by the TUI.\n- `.manigot/` (in the target project) — host-side tooling state only:\n  the committable `manigot.json` settings and the gitignored\n  `.manigot/jdi-status/` mg-jdi run state (removed when a job is finished,\n  deleted, or its orphaned worktree cleaned up). Agents must treat it like\n  any other tool-managed state: read the settings file if needed, never edit\n  either path by hand.\n\n## Commands\n- `make build` — build the image (skips if already built)\n- `make rebuild` — force rebuild with no cache, after a Claude Code / OpenCode update\n- `make mg` — build the host-side `bin/mg` binary\n- `make install` / `make uninstall` — symlink the single `mg` binary into\n  `PREFIX/bin` (default `~/.local/bin`)\n- `mg` — start an isolated session from inside any project directory; `docs/`\n  is optional (see Architecture above)\n- `mg --profile <name>` — same, but under the given subscription profile\n  (`claude-pro`/`zai`/`opencode-go`/`opencode-zen`/`opencode-zen-free`); `--tool` is accepted as a legacy alias\n- `mg profiles [name|add|rm]` — list the profiles (and which is the default),\n  set the default bare `mg` uses, pick it interactively (no name, on a TTY),\n  or manage your own user-defined profiles with `add`/`rm`\n  (stored in `config/profiles.json`)\n- `mg theme [name]` — show or set manigot's global OpenCode theme\n  (`OPENCODE_THEME`, shared across every OpenCode profile), or pick it\n  interactively (no name, on a TTY) from a reference list of OpenCode's known","lineStart":509,"lineEnd":638,"totalLines":773,"truncated":true}},"title":"docs/AGENTS.md","time":{"start":1787952140846,"end":1787952140849}},"id":"prt_04a4091a9001eIr1gfDHr75aJn","sessionID":"ses_fb5dcd7a6ffeSGBPKFVeVpziRm","messageID":"msg_04a4088e6001IEaiOYFgkBVokm"}}
