{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787952235246,"sessionID":"ses_fb5dcd7a6ffeSGBPKFVeVpziRm","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_470d6ff9788c472dba59efba","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/README.md","limit":80,"offset":1153},"output":"<path>/workspace/README.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1153: ## Listener\n1154: \n1155: `mg serve` is the listener: a long-running daemon exposing a **read-only**\n1156: control API over a registry of project roots, so any surface — a web UI, a\n1157: native GUI, a future CLI — can attach to it as a client, from localhost or\n1158: from a VPS. It is job one of the control-plane sequence; the API is read-only\n1159: by design (mutating endpoints, live run supervision with streamed logs, and\n1160: any frontend are later jobs — see the out-of-scope list in\n1161: [`docs/jobs/wood_listener-architecture/brief.md`](docs/jobs/wood_listener-architecture/brief.md)).\n1162: \n1163: **Registry.** An explicit config file of named project roots — no scanning, no\n1164: auto-adopting directories the daemon finds:\n1165: \n1166: ```bash\n1167: # <manigot checkout>/config/serve.json  (override with --registry)\n1168: {\"projects\": [{\"name\": \"my-project\", \"path\": \"/abs/project/root\"}, ...]}\n1169: ```\n1170: \n1171: `name` is required — the URL segment the project is served under, chosen by\n1172: you (a single URL-safe path segment, unique across the registry). Nothing is\n1173: auto-derived from the directory name. Registrations are read once at startup;\n1174: changing them means editing the file and restarting (v1). Each entry's `path`\n1175: must be an existing directory; a root without `docs/` is accepted and simply\n1176: lists no jobs.\n1177: \n1178: **Binding + auth.** The daemon binds `127.0.0.1:8080` by default and is\n1179: tokenless in that shape — the machine's own user is the trust boundary, as it\n1180: is for the CLI. A non-loopback bind (a VPS) **requires** a bearer token —\n1181: `--token`, else `$MG_SERVE_TOKEN` — or the daemon refuses to start; there is\n1182: no flag that turns that guard off. When a token is configured, every request\n1183: must carry `Authorization: Bearer <token>` (compared in constant time); a\n1184: missing or wrong token is a `401`. TLS is the reverse proxy's job (Caddy /\n1185: nginx) — the daemon always serves plain HTTP and never terminates TLS, the\n1186: only safe posture behind a proxy. A token without TLS is no protection.\n1187: \n1188: **API.** `GET /health` (version, docker image present, per-profile\n1189: readiness), `GET /projects`, `GET /projects/<p>/jobs` (id / status / stage /\n1190: type / date / title, plus per-job mg-jdi state),\n1191: `GET /projects/<p>/jobs/<j>/files/<brief|tasks|implementation|verdict>`\n1192: (raw markdown), `GET /projects/<p>/jobs/<j>/jdi` (status + `run.log` +\n1193: `session.log` tails), `GET /projects/<p>/jobs/<j>/diff` (the `mg diff` quick\n1194: eyeball, `?full=1` for the patch), and `GET /projects/<p>/agents`.\n1195: \n1196: **Security invariants** (non-negotiable): URL segments are validated as\n1197: plain identifiers and resolved only against the registry / discovered jobs /\n1198: the file whitelist — never joined into filesystem paths, and traversal in any\n1199: encoding is rejected; credentials are never returned in any response and never\n1200: logged (each request is audit-logged with timestamp, client, operation, auth\n1201: outcome and status — never the token); and mutating operations (a later job)\n1202: must serialize per project root via the `serve.ProjectLocks` pattern.\n1203: \n1204: ---\n1205: \n1206: ## Rebuilding\n1207: \n1208: When Claude Code or OpenCode releases an update worth taking:\n1209: \n1210: ```bash\n1211: cd manigot/\n1212: make rebuild\n1213: ```\n1214: \n1215: The image also ships `make` and the Go toolchain (Debian trixie's `golang-go`,\n1216: currently Go 1.24) so the host-side tool in `src/cmd/` can be built and tested\n1217: from inside a container. `GOTOOLCHAIN=local` is set, so if `src/go.mod` ever\n1218: requires a newer Go than the image has, the build fails loudly instead of\n1219: silently downloading one.\n1220: \n1221: The Go module cache is pre-warmed at build time from `src/go.mod` and\n1222: `src/go.sum`, which means `make mg` and `go test ./...` (from `src/`) work\n1223: inside the container without network access — but also that **bumping a\n1224: dependency requires a `make rebuild`**, otherwise the new module is missing\n1225: from the cache.\n\n(End of file - total 1225 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"## Listener\n\n`mg serve` is the listener: a long-running daemon exposing a **read-only**\ncontrol API over a registry of project roots, so any surface — a web UI, a\nnative GUI, a future CLI — can attach to it as a client, from localhost or\nfrom a VPS. It is job one of the control-plane sequence; the API is read-only\nby design (mutating endpoints, live run supervision with streamed logs, and\nany frontend are later jobs — see the out-of-scope list in\n[`docs/jobs/wood_listener-architecture/brief.md`](docs/jobs/wood_listener-architecture/brief.md)).\n\n**Registry.** An explicit config file of named project roots — no scanning, no\nauto-adopting directories the daemon finds:\n\n```bash\n# <manigot checkout>/config/serve.json  (override with --registry)\n{\"projects\": [{\"name\": \"my-project\", \"path\": \"/abs/project/root\"}, ...]}\n```\n\n`name` is required — the URL segment the project is served under, chosen by\nyou (a single URL-safe path segment, unique across the registry). Nothing is","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/README.md","text":"## Listener\n\n`mg serve` is the listener: a long-running daemon exposing a **read-only**\ncontrol API over a registry of project roots, so any surface — a web UI, a\nnative GUI, a future CLI — can attach to it as a client, from localhost or\nfrom a VPS. It is job one of the control-plane sequence; the API is read-only\nby design (mutating endpoints, live run supervision with streamed logs, and\nany frontend are later jobs — see the out-of-scope list in\n[`docs/jobs/wood_listener-architecture/brief.md`](docs/jobs/wood_listener-architecture/brief.md)).\n\n**Registry.** An explicit config file of named project roots — no scanning, no\nauto-adopting directories the daemon finds:\n\n```bash\n# <manigot checkout>/config/serve.json  (override with --registry)\n{\"projects\": [{\"name\": \"my-project\", \"path\": \"/abs/project/root\"}, ...]}\n```\n\n`name` is required — the URL segment the project is served under, chosen by\nyou (a single URL-safe path segment, unique across the registry). Nothing is\nauto-derived from the directory name. Registrations are read once at startup;\nchanging them means editing the file and restarting (v1). Each entry's `path`\nmust be an existing directory; a root without `docs/` is accepted and simply\nlists no jobs.\n\n**Binding + auth.** The daemon binds `127.0.0.1:8080` by default and is\ntokenless in that shape — the machine's own user is the trust boundary, as it\nis for the CLI. A non-loopback bind (a VPS) **requires** a bearer token —\n`--token`, else `$MG_SERVE_TOKEN` — or the daemon refuses to start; there is\nno flag that turns that guard off. When a token is configured, every request\nmust carry `Authorization: Bearer <token>` (compared in constant time); a\nmissing or wrong token is a `401`. TLS is the reverse proxy's job (Caddy /\nnginx) — the daemon always serves plain HTTP and never terminates TLS, the\nonly safe posture behind a proxy. A token without TLS is no protection.\n\n**API.** `GET /health` (version, docker image present, per-profile\nreadiness), `GET /projects`, `GET /projects/<p>/jobs` (id / status / stage /\ntype / date / title, plus per-job mg-jdi state),\n`GET /projects/<p>/jobs/<j>/files/<brief|tasks|implementation|verdict>`\n(raw markdown), `GET /projects/<p>/jobs/<j>/jdi` (status + `run.log` +\n`session.log` tails), `GET /projects/<p>/jobs/<j>/diff` (the `mg diff` quick\neyeball, `?full=1` for the patch), and `GET /projects/<p>/agents`.\n\n**Security invariants** (non-negotiable): URL segments are validated as\nplain identifiers and resolved only against the registry / discovered jobs /\nthe file whitelist — never joined into filesystem paths, and traversal in any\nencoding is rejected; credentials are never returned in any response and never\nlogged (each request is audit-logged with timestamp, client, operation, auth\noutcome and status — never the token); and mutating operations (a later job)\nmust serialize per project root via the `serve.ProjectLocks` pattern.\n\n---\n\n## Rebuilding\n\nWhen Claude Code or OpenCode releases an update worth taking:\n\n```bash\ncd manigot/\nmake rebuild\n```\n\nThe image also ships `make` and the Go toolchain (Debian trixie's `golang-go`,\ncurrently Go 1.24) so the host-side tool in `src/cmd/` can be built and tested\nfrom inside a container. `GOTOOLCHAIN=local` is set, so if `src/go.mod` ever\nrequires a newer Go than the image has, the build fails loudly instead of\nsilently downloading one.\n\nThe Go module cache is pre-warmed at build time from `src/go.mod` and\n`src/go.sum`, which means `make mg` and `go test ./...` (from `src/`) work\ninside the container without network access — but also that **bumping a\ndependency requires a `make rebuild`**, otherwise the new module is missing\nfrom the cache.","lineStart":1153,"lineEnd":1225,"totalLines":1225,"truncated":false}},"title":"README.md","time":{"start":1787952235241,"end":1787952235244}},"id":"prt_04a42018f001DK42Q4PNHHhG6L","sessionID":"ses_fb5dcd7a6ffeSGBPKFVeVpziRm","messageID":"msg_04a41f453001IH3VruUkYaTbyw"}}
