{"type":"text","timestamp":1787952888036,"sessionID":"ses_fb5ba93f2ffe9RBBAgSFG35dIN","part":{"id":"prt_04a4be2f2001PPT1Kw2DJfDcNX","messageID":"msg_04a4bd2fd001GKeFkdJ6qHfe02","sessionID":"ses_fb5ba93f2ffe9RBBAgSFG35dIN","type":"text","text":"Review complete. The verdict is committed (`8fde418 [farmer] verdict: ...`). The only remaining uncommitted change is `session.log` — my own session's live log, which the host-side sweep commits at session end (normal behavior).\n\n## Summary of the review\n\n**Process:** Read `brief.md`, `tasks.md`, `implementation.md`; confirmed the branch (`feature/farmer_part-2-of-web-ui-tui-path`); reviewed the full `git diff main...HEAD` (29 files, ~5,400 insertions); verified every API signature the new code depends on against the existing packages (`job`, `session`, `launch`, `git`, `config`, `agentlist`); confirmed the TASK-1 relocation was a pure move (test file byte-identical apart from renames); checked for import cycles and dangling references; read every new/changed test suite and the docs sync.\n\n**Verdict: NEEDS WORK** — one blocker, one task PARTIAL:\n\n- **TASK-7 (done endpoint) PARTIAL:** the squash-merge-conflict 409 body only carries `\"squash merge conflict — no automatic recovery attempted: <git msg>\"`. The task explicitly requires the response to *state that the job is already archived-and-committed and cannot be undone* — the implementation writes exactly that explanation, but `handleDoneJob` (mutate.go:424) discards the `out` buffer it lands in. A client retrying `done` after the 409 would hit a confusing \"brief.md not found\" (the dir was moved to `archive/`). Fix: surface the explanation in the 409 body.\n- All other 14 tasks PASS. The additive `FinishJobWithOptions` change is backward-compatible and well-tested; the one-shot primitive, all ten mutating endpoints with their exact ProjectLocks boundary, the SSE stream (including the graceful-shutdown drain participation the brief called out), the security/credentials/concurrency test suites, and the docs sync are complete and correct.\n\n**Non-blocking observations** (noted in the verdict, not blockers): edit-brief's `Warning` field is also populated on successful sweep commits (doc comment says failure-only); blank log lines are emitted as SSE comments rather than empty `data:` frames; and `main` carries a stray pre-existing commit `66d2524` (a root-level `implementation.md` from an early session) that is outside this job's diff and won't conflict with the merge, but is worth cleaning up.","time":{"start":1787952882418,"end":1787952888034}}}
