{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787952902138,"sessionID":"ses_fb5b402d5ffesBMXb1jVe3Cozl","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_d0a80f3a82d24060912a4149","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/farmer_part-2-of-web-ui-tui-path/verdict.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/farmer_part-2-of-web-ui-tui-path/verdict.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Verdict: part 2 of web ui tui path\n2: \n3: id: farmer\n4: status: open\n5: reviewer: deepseek-v4-flash\n6: date: 2026-08-28\n7: \n8: <!-- Produced by @reviewer and/or @security after implementation. -->\n9: \n10: ## Review\n11: \n12: TASK-1: PASS\n13: notes: Pure relocation verified: `src/internal/job/sessionlog.go` is byte-identical to\n14:   the removed `openSessionLog`/`sessionLog`/`ensureSessionLogFile` from\n15:   `src/cmd/mg/jdioutput.go` (modulo the exported renames), `cmd/mg/jdi.go` calls\n16:   `job.OpenSessionLog`/`job.EnsureSessionLogFile` with identical semantics (lines\n17:   591, 155), and the coverage moved (not rewritten) to\n18:   `src/internal/job/sessionlog_test.go` — same test names, same assertions, same\n19:   on-disk format (blank-line separator, \"=== <RFC3339> <agent> (attempt N) ===\"\n20:   header, trailing-newline guarantee on Close). No dangling references to the old\n21:   private names remain in cmd/mg (only a comment mention in internal/ui/detail.go).\n22: \n23: TASK-2: PARTIAL\n24: notes: `src/internal/session/oneshot.go` — the primitive correctly mirrors\n25:   cmd/mg/jdi.go's commandAgentRunner (ResolveProfile → ResolveRootFrom → CheckAuth\n26:   → BuildDockerInvocation → Run → SweepJobWorktree on ran), errors land in the\n27:   session.log section, the goroutine-outliving-the-request shape and the\n28:   concurrent-mg-jdi limitation are documented. Home in internal/session is the\n29:   right call (no import cycle: session→job only; serve→session). Marking PARTIAL\n30:   only because TASK-7's blocker below is what the done endpoint's conflict path\n31:   ships against; the one-shot primitive itself is complete and tested\n32:   (oneshot_test.go with a fake runner).\n33: \n34: TASK-3: PASS\n35: notes: `handleCreateJob` (mutate.go:118) — lock taken, `type` pre-validated\n36:   against CreateJob's accepted set (clean 400, validJobTypes:97), title required,\n37:   201 with job row + branch + worktreePath, out discarded. Tests cover git /\n38:   non-git / validation (mutate_test.go:54-153).\n39: \n40: TASK-4: PASS\n41: notes: `handleEditBrief` (mutate.go:181) — raw-body write of brief.md only (the\n42:   route is a literal, so tasks/implementation/verdict cannot be written), empty\n43:   and >1 MiB bodies are 400s, immediate `SweepJobWorktree` commit in the job's\n44:   own worktree, lock taken (reasoned addition). Git/non-git/validation tested.\n45:   Minor observation (not a blocker): the response `Warning` field is also\n46:   populated on a *successful* sweep commit (\"mg: committed leftover changes ...\"),\n47:   contradicting its own doc comment (\"set only when the post-write commit sweep\n48:   could not be attempted or failed\", mutate.go:158-161) — a cosmetic naming issue.\n49: \n50: TASK-5: PASS\n51: notes: `handleLaunchAgent` (mutate.go:245) — agent validated against\n52:   agentlist.Discover first (fast 404), optional profile validated via\n53:   ProfileByID defaulting to claude-pro, 202 returned, RunOneShot started in a\n54:   background goroutine, no lock. Tested (202 + session.log section appears;\n55:   unknown agent 404; bad profile 400).\n56: \n57: TASK-6: PASS\n58: notes: `handleLaunchJDI` (mutate.go:304) — 409 when ReadJDIStatus reports a live\n59:   running state (staleness correctly degrades to ok=false so a killed run does\n60:   not block relaunch), launch.Jdi detached subprocess (verified: launch.go:338,\n61:   cmd.Dir=projectRoot, stdio discarded, async reaped), no lock, 202. Tested with\n62:   JdiExe stubbed (mutate_test.go:295-323).\n63: \n64: TASK-7: PARTIAL\n65: notes: The additive FinishJobWithOptions change is correct and complete: zero-value\n66:   options behave byte-for-byte like FinishJob, NoConflictRecovery returns a\n67:   distinguishable ErrSquashMergeConflict without any prompt/rollback/git-solver\n68:   handoff (finish.go:268-279), existing CLI/TUI callers untouched, and the\n69:   \"verdict not approved\"/\"no verdict.md\" warnings require {\"force\": true} with the\n70:   CLI's own warning text in the 409 (mutate.go:416-419). The blocker: the task\n71:   explicitly requires that on a conflict \"the response should say so explicitly\n72:   rather than implying 'nothing happened'\" — i.e. the HTTP response must state\n73:   that the job is already archived-and-committed and cannot be undone. The\n74:   implementation writes exactly that explanation to the `out` buffer inside\n75:   FinishJobWithOptions (finish.go:269-276) but `handleDoneJob` discards `out`\n76:   (mutate.go:424) and returns only `err.Error()` = \"squash merge conflict — no\n77:   automatic recovery attempted: <git msg>\". A client reading the 409 body learns\n78:   the merge conflicted and no recovery was attempted, but not that the job dir is\n79:   already archived — and a naive retry of done then fails with a confusing\n80:   \"brief.md not found\" (the dir was moved to archive/). Fix: surface the\n81:   explanation in the 409 body (e.g. include `out.String()` or extend the wrapped\n82:   error with the archived-state wording).\n83: \n84: TASK-8: PASS\n85: notes: `handleDeleteJob` (mutate.go:451) — lock, pre-approved confirm (the HTTP\n86:   call is the confirmation), DeleteResult returned. Tested for git and non-git\n87:   projects and unknown jobs.\n88: \n89: TASK-9: PASS\n90: notes: `handlePushJob` (mutate.go:486) — lock, git.PushWithContext bounded by a\n91:   30s timeout (verified against the TUI's own hostGitTimeout = 30 * time.Second,\n92:   ui/app.go:202), git's own message in the structured error. Tested with no\n93:   remote (500) and a real bare remote (200).\n94: \n95: TASK-10: PASS\n96: notes: `handlePrune` (mutate.go:522) — top-level POST /prune (containers are not\n97:   project-partitioned), wraps session.PruneOrphans, reports removed+running, no\n98:   lock. Tested (docker absent → structured 500 with the docker error).\n99: \n100: TASK-11: PASS\n101: notes: GET /projects/{p}/orphans (DiscoverOrphans, read-only, no lock) and POST\n102:   /projects/{p}/orphans/{name}/delete (MatchOrphan + RemoveOrphansConfirmed for\n103:   one named orphan, under the lock — the reasoned addition, since\n104:   RemoveOrphansConfirmed calls git.WorktreePrune). Tested: list, delete-one,\n105:   untouched-other, 404.\n106: \n107: TASK-12: PASS\n108: notes: `stream.go` — SSE over net/http (no new dependency), starts at EOF / byte 0\n109:   for a missing file / ?from= offset, truncation resets to byte 0 with a fresh\n110:   start event, keepalive comment on idle, stop on client disconnect AND daemon\n111:   shutdown via the server-scoped shutdownCtx cancelled at the top of\n112:   Server.Shutdown (server.go:111-114) — the brief's explicitly-called-out\n113:   graceful-shutdown requirement. The two swept-in fixes (missing bytes/io imports\n114:   + undefined readAll; the {\"offset\":N} start payload) and the audit\n115:   middleware's Flush delegation (audit.go:50-54, without which every stream would\n116:   fail \"streaming unsupported\") are all correct. Tests cover live growth,\n117:   from-offset resume, file-appears-after-start, bad from, disconnect, and a\n118:   prompt shutdown drain. Minor observation (not a blocker): blank lines in\n119:   session.log are emitted as SSE comments (`: keepalive`) rather than empty\n120:   `data:` frames, so blank separator lines are invisible to EventSource consumers\n121:   — cosmetic.\n122: \n123: TASK-13: PASS\n124: notes: Hostile/encoded traversal segments added at every new URL position\n125:   ({project} on create, {job} on all mutating routes, {agent}, orphan {name}) with\n126:   a no-leak assertion (security_test.go:217-273), and the known-credential grep\n127:   re-run across every mutating endpoint's success and error envelopes plus the\n128:   audit log (credentials_test.go:131-191). Both invariants hold by inspection of\n129:   the handlers (all paths flow through the resolveProject/resolveJob/validSegment\n130:   choke points; no handler touches .env).\n131: \n132: TASK-14: PASS\n133: notes: concurrency_test.go pins the boundary end to end: create/edit-brief/done/\n134:   delete/push/orphan-delete block behind a held project lock, launch-agent/\n135:   launch-jdi/prune/reads complete immediately, and two different projects proceed\n136:   independently — the exact property the brief's Notes worried about. Matches the\n137:   shipped handler code (mutate.go: each mutating handler takes\n138:   s.locks.Lock(root) except launch-agent/launch-jdi/prune/reads).\n139: \n140: TASK-15: PASS\n141: notes: docs/AGENTS.md (+ its project-template mirror) document the mutating API,\n142:   the 202-then-poll/stream contract, the SSE endpoint, and the shipped ProjectLocks\n143:   boundary; README.md's command table + Listener section updated; docs/listener.md\n144:   marks job two DONE with a short annotation including the recorded\n145:   edit-brief+relaunch decision on NEEDS-HUMAN-INPUT; the `mg serve` help text no\n146:   longer claims read-only. All accurately describe what shipped.\n147: \n148: ## Security\n149: \n150: No new findings beyond the review notes. The two job-one invariants (zero path\n151: inputs; credentials never returned) are re-pinned across the whole mutating\n152: surface by TASK-13's tests. The auth/audit middleware chain is unchanged in\n153: structure; the statusRecorder.Flush addition is the only modification and is\n154: needed for SSE to work at all.\n155: \n156: One out-of-band observation (not this job's change, on `main`, not on this\n157: branch): `main` carries a stray commit 66d2524 \"[farmer] implementation: add\n158: summary\" adding a root-level `implementation.md` — an artifact of an early\n159: session that committed to the main worktree before this job's worktree existed.\n160: It is outside this job's diff (three-dot merge-base is c17938d) and does not\n161: conflict with this job's squash merge, but the human should clean it up when\n162: merging.\n163: \n164: ## Overall\n165: \n166: NEEDS WORK\n167: \n168: One blocker, in TASK-7: the done endpoint's squash-merge-conflict 409 body must\n169: explicitly state that the job is already archived-and-committed and cannot be\n170: undone (per the task's own requirement that \"the response should say so\n171: explicitly rather than implying 'nothing happened'\"). Currently the explanatory\n172: text is written to an `out` buffer that `handleDoneJob` discards\n173: (src/internal/serve/mutate.go:424), so the 409 body only says \"squash merge\n174: conflict — no automatic recovery attempted: <git msg>\". Fix: include the\n175: explanation in the 409 error body (e.g. append `out.String()` or extend the\n176: wrapped error with the archived-state wording), ideally with a test asserting\n177: the body mentions the archive. Everything else — the relocation, the one-shot\n178: primitive, all ten mutating endpoints, the SSE stream with its shutdown\n179: participation, the security/credentials/concurrency test suites, and the docs\n180: sync — is complete, correct, and in scope.\n\n(End of file - total 180 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Verdict: part 2 of web ui tui path\n\nid: farmer\nstatus: open\nreviewer: deepseek-v4-flash\ndate: 2026-08-28\n\n<!-- Produced by @reviewer and/or @security after implementation. -->\n\n## Review\n\nTASK-1: PASS\nnotes: Pure relocation verified: `src/internal/job/sessionlog.go` is byte-identical to\n  the removed `openSessionLog`/`sessionLog`/`ensureSessionLogFile` from\n  `src/cmd/mg/jdioutput.go` (modulo the exported renames), `cmd/mg/jdi.go` calls\n  `job.OpenSessionLog`/`job.EnsureSessionLogFile` with identical semantics (lines\n  591, 155), and the coverage moved (not rewritten) to\n  `src/internal/job/sessionlog_test.go` — same test names, same assertions, same\n  on-disk format (blank-line separator, \"=== <RFC3339> <agent> (attempt N) ===\"\n  header, trailing-newline guarantee on Close). No dangling references to the old","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/farmer_part-2-of-web-ui-tui-path/verdict.md","text":"# Verdict: part 2 of web ui tui path\n\nid: farmer\nstatus: open\nreviewer: deepseek-v4-flash\ndate: 2026-08-28\n\n<!-- Produced by @reviewer and/or @security after implementation. -->\n\n## Review\n\nTASK-1: PASS\nnotes: Pure relocation verified: `src/internal/job/sessionlog.go` is byte-identical to\n  the removed `openSessionLog`/`sessionLog`/`ensureSessionLogFile` from\n  `src/cmd/mg/jdioutput.go` (modulo the exported renames), `cmd/mg/jdi.go` calls\n  `job.OpenSessionLog`/`job.EnsureSessionLogFile` with identical semantics (lines\n  591, 155), and the coverage moved (not rewritten) to\n  `src/internal/job/sessionlog_test.go` — same test names, same assertions, same\n  on-disk format (blank-line separator, \"=== <RFC3339> <agent> (attempt N) ===\"\n  header, trailing-newline guarantee on Close). No dangling references to the old\n  private names remain in cmd/mg (only a comment mention in internal/ui/detail.go).\n\nTASK-2: PARTIAL\nnotes: `src/internal/session/oneshot.go` — the primitive correctly mirrors\n  cmd/mg/jdi.go's commandAgentRunner (ResolveProfile → ResolveRootFrom → CheckAuth\n  → BuildDockerInvocation → Run → SweepJobWorktree on ran), errors land in the\n  session.log section, the goroutine-outliving-the-request shape and the\n  concurrent-mg-jdi limitation are documented. Home in internal/session is the\n  right call (no import cycle: session→job only; serve→session). Marking PARTIAL\n  only because TASK-7's blocker below is what the done endpoint's conflict path\n  ships against; the one-shot primitive itself is complete and tested\n  (oneshot_test.go with a fake runner).\n\nTASK-3: PASS\nnotes: `handleCreateJob` (mutate.go:118) — lock taken, `type` pre-validated\n  against CreateJob's accepted set (clean 400, validJobTypes:97), title required,\n  201 with job row + branch + worktreePath, out discarded. Tests cover git /\n  non-git / validation (mutate_test.go:54-153).\n\nTASK-4: PASS\nnotes: `handleEditBrief` (mutate.go:181) — raw-body write of brief.md only (the\n  route is a literal, so tasks/implementation/verdict cannot be written), empty\n  and >1 MiB bodies are 400s, immediate `SweepJobWorktree` commit in the job's\n  own worktree, lock taken (reasoned addition). Git/non-git/validation tested.\n  Minor observation (not a blocker): the response `Warning` field is also\n  populated on a *successful* sweep commit (\"mg: committed leftover changes ...\"),\n  contradicting its own doc comment (\"set only when the post-write commit sweep\n  could not be attempted or failed\", mutate.go:158-161) — a cosmetic naming issue.\n\nTASK-5: PASS\nnotes: `handleLaunchAgent` (mutate.go:245) — agent validated against\n  agentlist.Discover first (fast 404), optional profile validated via\n  ProfileByID defaulting to claude-pro, 202 returned, RunOneShot started in a\n  background goroutine, no lock. Tested (202 + session.log section appears;\n  unknown agent 404; bad profile 400).\n\nTASK-6: PASS\nnotes: `handleLaunchJDI` (mutate.go:304) — 409 when ReadJDIStatus reports a live\n  running state (staleness correctly degrades to ok=false so a killed run does\n  not block relaunch), launch.Jdi detached subprocess (verified: launch.go:338,\n  cmd.Dir=projectRoot, stdio discarded, async reaped), no lock, 202. Tested with\n  JdiExe stubbed (mutate_test.go:295-323).\n\nTASK-7: PARTIAL\nnotes: The additive FinishJobWithOptions change is correct and complete: zero-value\n  options behave byte-for-byte like FinishJob, NoConflictRecovery returns a\n  distinguishable ErrSquashMergeConflict without any prompt/rollback/git-solver\n  handoff (finish.go:268-279), existing CLI/TUI callers untouched, and the\n  \"verdict not approved\"/\"no verdict.md\" warnings require {\"force\": true} with the\n  CLI's own warning text in the 409 (mutate.go:416-419). The blocker: the task\n  explicitly requires that on a conflict \"the response should say so explicitly\n  rather than implying 'nothing happened'\" — i.e. the HTTP response must state\n  that the job is already archived-and-committed and cannot be undone. The\n  implementation writes exactly that explanation to the `out` buffer inside\n  FinishJobWithOptions (finish.go:269-276) but `handleDoneJob` discards `out`\n  (mutate.go:424) and returns only `err.Error()` = \"squash merge conflict — no\n  automatic recovery attempted: <git msg>\". A client reading the 409 body learns\n  the merge conflicted and no recovery was attempted, but not that the job dir is\n  already archived — and a naive retry of done then fails with a confusing\n  \"brief.md not found\" (the dir was moved to archive/). Fix: surface the\n  explanation in the 409 body (e.g. include `out.String()` or extend the wrapped\n  error with the archived-state wording).\n\nTASK-8: PASS\nnotes: `handleDeleteJob` (mutate.go:451) — lock, pre-approved confirm (the HTTP\n  call is the confirmation), DeleteResult returned. Tested for git and non-git\n  projects and unknown jobs.\n\nTASK-9: PASS\nnotes: `handlePushJob` (mutate.go:486) — lock, git.PushWithContext bounded by a\n  30s timeout (verified against the TUI's own hostGitTimeout = 30 * time.Second,\n  ui/app.go:202), git's own message in the structured error. Tested with no\n  remote (500) and a real bare remote (200).\n\nTASK-10: PASS\nnotes: `handlePrune` (mutate.go:522) — top-level POST /prune (containers are not\n  project-partitioned), wraps session.PruneOrphans, reports removed+running, no\n  lock. Tested (docker absent → structured 500 with the docker error).\n\nTASK-11: PASS\nnotes: GET /projects/{p}/orphans (DiscoverOrphans, read-only, no lock) and POST\n  /projects/{p}/orphans/{name}/delete (MatchOrphan + RemoveOrphansConfirmed for\n  one named orphan, under the lock — the reasoned addition, since\n  RemoveOrphansConfirmed calls git.WorktreePrune). Tested: list, delete-one,\n  untouched-other, 404.\n\nTASK-12: PASS\nnotes: `stream.go` — SSE over net/http (no new dependency), starts at EOF / byte 0\n  for a missing file / ?from= offset, truncation resets to byte 0 with a fresh\n  start event, keepalive comment on idle, stop on client disconnect AND daemon\n  shutdown via the server-scoped shutdownCtx cancelled at the top of\n  Server.Shutdown (server.go:111-114) — the brief's explicitly-called-out\n  graceful-shutdown requirement. The two swept-in fixes (missing bytes/io imports\n  + undefined readAll; the {\"offset\":N} start payload) and the audit\n  middleware's Flush delegation (audit.go:50-54, without which every stream would\n  fail \"streaming unsupported\") are all correct. Tests cover live growth,\n  from-offset resume, file-appears-after-start, bad from, disconnect, and a\n  prompt shutdown drain. Minor observation (not a blocker): blank lines in\n  session.log are emitted as SSE comments (`: keepalive`) rather than empty\n  `data:` frames, so blank separator lines are invisible to EventSource consumers\n  — cosmetic.\n\nTASK-13: PASS\nnotes: Hostile/encoded traversal segments added at every new URL position\n  ({project} on create, {job} on all mutating routes, {agent}, orphan {name}) with\n  a no-leak assertion (security_test.go:217-273), and the known-credential grep\n  re-run across every mutating endpoint's success and error envelopes plus the\n  audit log (credentials_test.go:131-191). Both invariants hold by inspection of\n  the handlers (all paths flow through the resolveProject/resolveJob/validSegment\n  choke points; no handler touches .env).\n\nTASK-14: PASS\nnotes: concurrency_test.go pins the boundary end to end: create/edit-brief/done/\n  delete/push/orphan-delete block behind a held project lock, launch-agent/\n  launch-jdi/prune/reads complete immediately, and two different projects proceed\n  independently — the exact property the brief's Notes worried about. Matches the\n  shipped handler code (mutate.go: each mutating handler takes\n  s.locks.Lock(root) except launch-agent/launch-jdi/prune/reads).\n\nTASK-15: PASS\nnotes: docs/AGENTS.md (+ its project-template mirror) document the mutating API,\n  the 202-then-poll/stream contract, the SSE endpoint, and the shipped ProjectLocks\n  boundary; README.md's command table + Listener section updated; docs/listener.md\n  marks job two DONE with a short annotation including the recorded\n  edit-brief+relaunch decision on NEEDS-HUMAN-INPUT; the `mg serve` help text no\n  longer claims read-only. All accurately describe what shipped.\n\n## Security\n\nNo new findings beyond the review notes. The two job-one invariants (zero path\ninputs; credentials never returned) are re-pinned across the whole mutating\nsurface by TASK-13's tests. The auth/audit middleware chain is unchanged in\nstructure; the statusRecorder.Flush addition is the only modification and is\nneeded for SSE to work at all.\n\nOne out-of-band observation (not this job's change, on `main`, not on this\nbranch): `main` carries a stray commit 66d2524 \"[farmer] implementation: add\nsummary\" adding a root-level `implementation.md` — an artifact of an early\nsession that committed to the main worktree before this job's worktree existed.\nIt is outside this job's diff (three-dot merge-base is c17938d) and does not\nconflict with this job's squash merge, but the human should clean it up when\nmerging.\n\n## Overall\n\nNEEDS WORK\n\nOne blocker, in TASK-7: the done endpoint's squash-merge-conflict 409 body must\nexplicitly state that the job is already archived-and-committed and cannot be\nundone (per the task's own requirement that \"the response should say so\nexplicitly rather than implying 'nothing happened'\"). Currently the explanatory\ntext is written to an `out` buffer that `handleDoneJob` discards\n(src/internal/serve/mutate.go:424), so the 409 body only says \"squash merge\nconflict — no automatic recovery attempted: <git msg>\". Fix: include the\nexplanation in the 409 error body (e.g. append `out.String()` or extend the\nwrapped error with the archived-state wording), ideally with a test asserting\nthe body mentions the archive. Everything else — the relocation, the one-shot\nprimitive, all ten mutating endpoints, the SSE stream with its shutdown\nparticipation, the security/credentials/concurrency test suites, and the docs\nsync — is complete, correct, and in scope.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":180,"totalLines":180,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/farmer_part-2-of-web-ui-tui-path/verdict.md","time":{"start":1787952902129,"end":1787952902136}},"id":"prt_04a4c2f790016NTE8NJzEAaMtb","sessionID":"ses_fb5b402d5ffesBMXb1jVe3Cozl","messageID":"msg_04a4c26ae001rzoMk2ceqLBQ1b"}}
