{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787953070464,"sessionID":"ses_fb5b402d5ffesBMXb1jVe3Cozl","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_6996b41824f04dd6ad8286e2","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/farmer_part-2-of-web-ui-tui-path/verdict.md","content":"# Verdict: part 2 of web ui tui path\n\nid: farmer\nstatus: open\nreviewer: deepseek-v4-flash\ndate: 2026-08-28\n\n<!-- Produced by @reviewer and/or @security after implementation. -->\n\n## Review\n\nRe-review after the previous verdict (`8fde418`, NEEDS WORK). Since that\nverdict the only commit on this branch is a host-side sweep of the job's\n`session.log` (`50ce948`) — **no code changed**. Every finding below is\ntherefore against the same code the previous reviewer assessed; I re-verified\nthe whole surface independently rather than trusting the prior notes.\n\nTASK-1: PASS\nnotes: Pure relocation verified against the diff: `src/internal/job/sessionlog.go`\n  is byte-identical to the removed `openSessionLog`/`sessionLog`/\n  `ensureSessionLogFile` from `src/cmd/mg/jdioutput.go` (modulo the exported\n  renames `SessionLog`/`OpenSessionLog`/`EnsureSessionLogFile`), `cmd/mg/jdi.go`\n  calls `job.OpenSessionLog`/`job.EnsureSessionLogFile` with identical\n  semantics (jdi.go:591, 155), and the coverage moved (not rewritten) to\n  `src/internal/job/sessionlog_test.go` — same test names and assertions, same\n  on-disk format (blank-line separator, \"=== <RFC3339> <agent> (attempt N) ===\"\n  header, trailing-newline guarantee on Close). No dangling references to the\n  old private names remain in cmd/mg.\n\nTASK-2: PASS\nnotes: `src/internal/session/oneshot.go` — the primitive mirrors cmd/mg/jdi.go's\n  commandAgentRunner shape (ResolveProfile → ResolveRootFrom → CheckAuth →\n  BuildDockerInvocation → Run → SweepJobWorktree on ran), the session.log\n  section opens at attempt 1, runner errors land in the same section\n  (RunOneShot's only reporting channel once the HTTP request has returned),\n  and the goroutine-outliving-the-request shape plus the concurrent-mg-jdi\n  limitation are documented. Home in internal/session is right (no import\n  cycle; serve→session→job). Tested with a fake runner (oneshot_test.go:\n  section format, trailing newline, error-into-log, multiple appends).\n  Marked PARTIAL last time only because TASK-7's blocker shipped against it;\n  the primitive itself is complete.\n\nTASK-3: PASS\nnotes: `handleCreateJob` (mutate.go:118) — lock taken, `type` pre-validated\n  against CreateJob's accepted set (clean 400 via validJobTypes:97), title\n  required, 201 with job row + branch + worktreePath. `CreateJob(root, title,\n  CreateOptions{Type, BaseBranchOverride}, out)` signature verified against\n  create.go:75. Tests cover git / non-git / validation (mutate_test.go:54-153).\n\nTASK-4: PASS\nnotes: `handleEditBrief` (mutate.go:181) — raw-body replace of brief.md only\n  (the PUT route is a literal, so tasks/implementation/verdict cannot be\n  written), empty and >1 MiB bodies are 400s, immediate SweepJobWorktree\n  commit in the job's own worktree, lock taken (reasoned addition, correct:\n  the sweep commits). The worktree resolution gate\n  (WorktreeForBranch → sweep → warning fallback) handles git / non-git /\n  no-worktree states. Git/non-git/validation tested.\n  Minor observation (not a blocker, carried from the previous review): the\n  response `Warning` field is also populated on a *successful* sweep commit\n  (\"mg: committed leftover changes ...\", mutate.go:219-221), contradicting its\n  own doc comment (\"set only when the post-write commit sweep could not be\n  attempted or failed\") — a cosmetic naming issue.\n\nTASK-5: PASS\nnotes: `handleLaunchAgent` (mutate.go:245) — agent validated against\n  agentlist.Discover first (fast 404), segment validated by validSegment, the\n  optional profile validated via ProfileByID defaulting to claude-pro, 202\n  returned, RunOneShot started in a background goroutine, no lock (per the\n  brief's Notes — correct). Tested (202 + session.log section appears; unknown\n  agent 404; bad profile 400).\n\nTASK-6: PASS\nnotes: `handleLaunchJDI` (mutate.go:304) — 409 when ReadJDIStatus reports a\n  live running state (staleness correctly degrades to ok=false via\n  jdistatus.go:100, so a killed run does not block relaunch), launch.Jdi is a\n  detached subprocess (launch.go:338), no lock, 202. Tested with JdiExe\n  stubbed (mutate_test.go:295-323).\n\nTASK-7: FAIL\nnotes: The additive FinishJobWithOptions change is correct and complete:\n  zero-value options behave byte-for-byte like FinishJob (finish_test.go:238),\n  NoConflictRecovery returns a distinguishable ErrSquashMergeConflict without\n  any prompt/rollback/git-solver handoff (finish.go:268-279), existing\n  CLI/TUI callers untouched, and the \"verdict not approved\"/\"no verdict.md\"\n  warnings require {\"force\": true} with the CLI's own warning text in the 409\n  (mutate.go:416-419, doneVerdictWarning:364). **The blocker from the previous\n  verdict is NOT fixed.** The task requires that on a conflict \"the response\n  should say so explicitly rather than implying 'nothing happened'\" — i.e. the\n  HTTP 409 body must state that the job is already archived-and-committed in\n  its own worktree and cannot be undone. That explanation is written to the\n  `out` buffer inside FinishJobWithOptions (finish.go:269-276) but\n  `handleDoneJob` still discards `out` (mutate.go:424) and returns only\n  `err.Error()` = \"squash merge conflict — no automatic recovery attempted:\n  <git msg>\". A client reading the 409 learns the merge conflicted, not that\n  the job dir was moved to docs/jobs/archive/ — and a naive retry of done then\n  fails with the confusing \"brief.md not found\" (finish.go:155-157, the dir\n  was renamed). The test TestHandleDoneJobConflictIsStructured409\n  (mutate_test.go:385-411) still only asserts the body contains \"squash merge\n  conflict\", not the archived-state wording.\n\nTASK-8: PASS\nnotes: `handleDeleteJob` (mutate.go:451) — lock, pre-approved confirm (the\n  HTTP call is the confirmation, mirroring the TUI's yesConfirm precedent),\n  DeleteResult returned. Tested for git and non-git projects and unknown jobs.\n\nTASK-9: PASS\nnotes: `handlePushJob` (mutate.go:486) — lock, git.PushWithContext bounded by\n  a 30s timeout (pushTimeout:479, matching the TUI's own hostGitTimeout),\n  git's own message in the structured error. Tested with no remote (500 with\n  the origin error) and a real bare remote (200).\n\nTASK-10: PASS\nnotes: `handlePrune` (mutate.go:522) — top-level POST /prune (containers are\n  not project-partitioned), wraps session.PruneOrphans, reports removed +\n  running, no lock. Tested (docker absent → structured 500 with the docker\n  error — the meaningful contract being a JSON envelope, never a silent\n  no-op).\n\nTASK-11: PASS\nnotes: GET /projects/{p}/orphans (DiscoverOrphans, read-only, no lock) and\n  POST /projects/{p}/orphans/{name}/delete (MatchOrphan + one named orphan via\n  RemoveOrphansConfirmed, under the lock — the reasoned addition, since\n  RemoveOrphansConfirmed calls git.WorktreePrune). Signatures verified\n  (orphan.go:59/130/195). Tested: list, delete-one, untouched-other, 404.\n\nTASK-12: PASS\nnotes: `stream.go` — SSE over net/http (no new dependency), starts at EOF /\n  byte 0 for a missing file / ?from= offset, truncation resets to byte 0 with\n  a fresh start event ({\"offset\":N} payload), keepalive comment on idle, stop\n  on client disconnect AND daemon shutdown via the server-scoped shutdownCtx\n  cancelled at the top of Server.Shutdown (server.go:111-114) — the brief's\n  explicitly-called-out graceful-shutdown requirement, and the drain path in\n  cmd/mg/serve.go:154-163 is wired to it. The audit middleware's Flush\n  delegation (audit.go:50-54) is correct and necessary (without it the\n  statusRecorder would break the w.(http.Flusher) assertion and every stream\n  would fail \"streaming unsupported\"). Tests cover live growth, from-offset\n  resume, file-appears-after-start, bad from, disconnect, and a prompt\n  shutdown drain. Minor observation (not a blocker, carried from the previous\n  review): blank lines in session.log are emitted as `: keepalive` comments\n  rather than empty data frames, so blank separator lines are invisible to\n  EventSource consumers — cosmetic.\n\nTASK-13: PASS\nnotes: security_test.go adds hostile/encoded traversal segments at every new\n  URL position ({project} on create, {job} on all six mutating routes, {agent},\n  orphan {name}) with a no-leak assertion, and credentials_test.go re-runs the\n  known-credential grep across every mutating endpoint's success and error\n  envelopes (create/edit-brief/launch-agent/launch-jdi/done/push/prune/orphans\n  list+delete/stream). Both invariants hold by inspection of the handlers — all\n  paths flow through resolveProject/resolveJob/validSegment and no handler\n  touches .env.\n\nTASK-14: PASS\nnotes: concurrency_test.go pins the boundary end to end: create/edit-brief/\n  done/delete/push/orphan-delete block behind a held project lock (and proceed\n  once released), launch-agent/launch-jdi/prune/reads complete immediately,\n  and two different projects proceed independently — the exact property the\n  brief's Notes worried about. Matches the shipped handler code: every\n  mutating handler takes s.locks.Lock(root) except launch-agent/launch-jdi/\n  prune/reads.\n\nTASK-15: PASS\nnotes: docs/AGENTS.md (+ its project-template mirror) document the mutating\n  API, the 202-then-poll/stream contract, the SSE endpoint, and the shipped\n  ProjectLocks boundary (which ops lock, which don't, and why); README.md's\n  command table + Listener section updated the same way; docs/listener.md\n  marks job two DONE with a short annotation including the recorded\n  edit-brief+relaunch decision on NEEDS-HUMAN-INPUT; the `mg serve` help text\n  no longer claims read-only (serve.go:59-65). All accurately describe what\n  shipped.\n\n## Security\n\nNo new findings beyond the review notes. The two job-one invariants (zero path\ninputs; credentials never returned) are re-pinned across the whole mutating\nsurface by TASK-13's tests. The auth/audit middleware chain is unchanged in\nstructure; the statusRecorder.Flush addition is the only modification and is\nneeded for SSE to work at all. The stream handler's `start`/`data` frames\ncarry only log content and byte offsets; the `?from=` parameter is validated\nbefore any SSE headers are written.\n\nOne out-of-band observation (not this job's change, on `main`, not on this\nbranch): `main` still carries the stray commit 66d2524 \"[farmer] implementation:\nadd summary\" adding a root-level `implementation.md` — an artifact of an early\nsession that committed to the main worktree before this job's worktree existed.\nIt is outside this job's diff and does not conflict with this job's squash\nmerge, but the human should clean it up when merging.\n\n## Overall\n\nNEEDS WORK\n\nThe single blocker from the previous verdict remains unaddressed — no code\nchanged on this branch since `8fde418` (only the job's `session.log` was\nswept). Blocking item, in TASK-7: the done endpoint's squash-merge-conflict\n409 body must explicitly state that the job is already archived-and-committed\nin its own worktree and cannot be undone (per the task's own requirement that\n\"the response should say so explicitly rather than implying 'nothing\nhappened'\"). Currently `handleDoneJob` (src/internal/serve/mutate.go:424-430)\ndiscards the explanatory `out` buffer and the 409 body only says \"squash merge\nconflict — no automatic recovery attempted: <git msg>\"; a retry of done then\nfails confusingly with \"brief.md not found\". Fix: include the explanation in\nthe 409 error body (e.g. append `out.String()`, or extend the wrapped error\nwith the archived-state wording — the explanation already exists verbatim in\nfinish.go:269-276), and extend TestHandleDoneJobConflictIsStructured409 to\nassert the body mentions the archive. Everything else — the relocation, the\none-shot primitive, all ten mutating endpoints, the SSE stream with its\nshutdown participation, the security/credentials/concurrency test suites, and\nthe docs sync — is complete, correct, and in scope."},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/farmer_part-2-of-web-ui-tui-path/verdict.md","exists":true,"truncated":false},"title":"docs/jobs/farmer_part-2-of-web-ui-tui-path/verdict.md","time":{"start":1787953070449,"end":1787953070463}},"id":"prt_04a4e7e22001VRKVrtTz023sNW","sessionID":"ses_fb5b402d5ffesBMXb1jVe3Cozl","messageID":"msg_04a4e6a44001Tb20QAk6YMaDtK"}}
