{"type":"text","timestamp":1787953079752,"sessionID":"ses_fb5b402d5ffesBMXb1jVe3Cozl","part":{"id":"prt_04a4ed93c001lDZXsm43m67nJC","messageID":"msg_04a4ecfd6001NGLz341niKxa6r","sessionID":"ses_fb5b402d5ffesBMXb1jVe3Cozl","type":"text","text":"Review complete. Verdict committed as `8910f1e`.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Overall: NEEDS WORK** — one blocker, unchanged from the previous review.\n\n**Key finding:** This is a re-review. Since the previous verdict (`8fde418`, NEEDS WORK), **no code changed on the branch** — the only commit after it (`50ce948`) was a host-side sweep of the job's `session.log`. I re-verified the entire implementation independently rather than trusting the prior notes.\n\n**TASK-7 FAIL (the blocker):** The done endpoint's squash-merge-conflict 409 body still doesn't state that the job is already archived-and-committed and cannot be undone — which the task explicitly requires (\"the response should say so explicitly rather than implying 'nothing happened'\"). In `src/internal/serve/mutate.go:424-430`, `handleDoneJob` discards the `out` buffer (which contains the archived-state explanation written at `finish.go:269-276`) and returns only `err.Error()` = \"squash merge conflict — no automatic recovery attempted: \\<git msg\\>\". A client reading the 409 can't tell the job dir was moved to `docs/jobs/archive/`, and a naive retry of `done` then fails confusingly with \"brief.md not found\". The test `TestHandleDoneJobConflictIsStructured409` only asserts \"squash merge conflict\" appears, not the archive wording. Fix: append `out.String()` (or extend the wrapped error) into the 409 body, plus a test asserting the body mentions the archive.\n\n**Everything else passes** after independent verification: the byte-identical session.log relocation (TASK-1), the one-shot detached runner with error-into-session.log reporting (TASK-2), all ten mutating endpoints with the correct ProjectLocks boundary (TASK-3–11), the SSE stream with its shutdown-context drain participation and the required audit-middleware `Flush` delegation (TASK-12), the security/credentials/concurrency suites (TASK-13/14), and the docs sync (TASK-15). Scope is clean — nothing changed outside the task list.\n\nTwo non-blocking observations carried from the previous review (both cosmetic): the edit-brief `Warning` field is populated on a *successful* sweep commit, and blank session.log separator lines are emitted as `: keepalive` SSE comments rather than empty data frames.","time":{"start":1787953076540,"end":1787953079750}}}
